          "root_comment_id": 4549039699,
          "thread_id": "PRRT_kwDOPmMU8s62kR_C",
          "type": "inline_review_comment",
          "author": "gemini-code-assist[bot]",
          "path": "core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/core/prefetch/ParquetFileLayout.java",
          "line": 59,
          "diff_hunk": "code rowGroups} is null\n    * @throws IllegalArgumentException if the index of a row group differs from its position in\n    *     {@code rowGroups}, or a row group starts before the previous one ends\n    */\n   static ParquetFileLayout create(\n       long schemaFingerprint, ImmutableList<ParquetRowGroup> rowGroups) {\n+    checkNotNull(rowGroups, \"rowGroups cannot be null\");\n     long endOffset = 0;",
          "body": "![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)\n\nAccording to the repository guidelines and general rules, we should avoid adding explicit null checks (like `Preconditions.checkNotNull`) in private or package-private methods if the parameter is immediately dereferenced on the first lines, as it will already fail fast with a `NullPointerException`. Explicit boundary checks should be reserved for public methods.\n\nIn `ParquetFileLayout.create`, which is package-private, `rowGroups` is immediately dereferenced on line 60 (`rowGroups.size()`). Therefore, the explicit `checkNotNull` check on line 58 is redundant and can be removed.\n\nWe should also update the corresponding test `create_nullRowGroups_throwsNullPointerException` in `ParquetFileLayoutTest.java` to not assert on the specific exception message.\n\n```suggestion\n    long endOffset = 0;\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>References</summary>\n\n1. Fail-Fast: Validate inputs at the boundary (public methods) immediately. <sup>([link](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gcs-analytics-core/blob/main/.gemini/styleguide.md))</sup>\n2. Avoid adding explicit null checks (like Preconditions.checkNotNull) in private or package-private methods if the parameter is immediately dereferenced on the first lines, as it will already fail fast with a NullPointerException. Reserve explicit boundary checks for public methods.\n</details>",
          "created_at": "2026-11-12T10:12:38Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gcs-analytics-core/pull/500#discussion_r4549039699"
        },
        {
          "id": "pull_comment:4549039733",
          "comment_id": 4549039733,
          "root_comment_id": 4549039733,
          "thread_id": "PRRT_kwDOPmMU8s62kR_i",
          "type": "inline_review_comment",
          "author": "gemini-code-assist[bot]",
          "path": "core/src/test/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/core/prefetch/ParquetFileLayoutTest.java",
          "line": 38,
          "diff_hunk": "@@ -27,6 +27,16 @@\n \n class ParquetFileLayoutTest {\n \n+  @Test\n+  void create_nullRowGroups_throwsNullPointerException() {\n+    NullPointerException e =\n+        assertThrows(\n+            NullPointerException.class,\n+            () -> ParquetFileLayout.create(/* schemaFingerprint= */ 7L, null));\n+\n+    assertThat(e).hasMessageThat().isEqualTo(\"rowGroups cannot be null\");\n+  }",
          "body": "![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)\n\nSince we are removing the redundant `checkNotNull` check in `ParquetFileLayout.create` (as the parameter is immediately dereferenced), the thrown `NullPointerException` will no longer have the specific message `\"rowGroups cannot be null\"`. We should update this test to only assert that a `NullPointerException` is thrown, without asserting on the specific message.\n\n```suggestion\n    assertThrows(\n        NullPointerException.class,\n        () -> ParquetFileLayout.create(/* schemaFingerprint= */ 7L, null));\n```",
